  "contribution": {
    "value": "HarmBench is a standardized red-teaming benchmark with 510 harmful behaviors across 4 functional categories used to compare 18 attack methods on 33 LLMs, and the paper introduces R2D2, an efficient adversarial training defense.",
    "ev": {
      "page": 1,
      "section": "Abstract",
      "quote": "we introduce HarmBench, a standardized evaluation framework for automated red teaming. We identify several desirable properties previously unaccounted for in red teaming evaluations and systematically design HarmBench to meet these criteria. Using HarmBench, we conduct a largescale comparison of 18 red teaming methods and 33 target LLMs",
      "bbox": [
        73.51171875,
        222.36328125,
        273.6994323730469,
        472.5460510253906
      ],
      "block_id": "/page/0/Text/4"
    }
  },
